@page "/"
@layout PublicLayout

<PageTitle>Query Gate · Governed SQL access</PageTitle>

<div class="landing-wrap">
    <section class="landing-hero">
        <div class="landing-copy">
            <span class="landing-eyebrow"><Icon Name="shield" /> A safer way to work with SQL Server</span>
            <h1>Give your team access.<br /><span>Keep the guardrails.</span></h1>
            <p>Query Gate brings database access, approvals and auditing together in one workspace. Run the queries you need with controls built in.</p>
            <div class="landing-actions">
                <AuthorizeView>
                    <Authorized><a class="btn btn-primary landing-button" href="/query">Open query workspace <Icon Name="chevron" /></a></Authorized>
                    <NotAuthorized><a class="btn btn-primary landing-button" href="/Account/Login">Sign in to Query Gate <Icon Name="chevron" /></a></NotAuthorized>
                </AuthorizeView>
                <a class="btn landing-button" href="/documentation">Explore documentation</a>
            </div>
            <div class="landing-note">Open source <span> / </span> Built for SQL Server <span> / </span> Powered by .NET</div>
        </div>
        <div class="landing-preview" aria-label="Query Gate workflow">
            <div class="preview-top"><span class="preview-dot"></span><span class="preview-dot"></span><span class="preview-dot"></span><span class="preview-title">QUERY WORKSPACE</span></div>
            <div class="preview-body">
                <div class="preview-heading"><span class="preview-icon"><Icon Name="terminal" /></span><div><strong>SQL workspace</strong><small>One governed doorway to your data</small></div></div>
                <div class="preview-code"><span>01</span> SELECT *<br /><span>02</span> FROM dbo.Orders<br /><span>03</span> WHERE Status = 'Open';</div>
                <div class="preview-check"><Icon Name="check" /><div><strong>Checked before execution</strong><small>Permissions verified. Activity recorded.</small></div></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="landing-features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
        <div class="landing-section-head"><span class="landing-kicker">CONTROL WITHOUT THE FRICTION</span><h2 id="features-title">A better path from request to query.</h2><p>Give people a practical workspace and administrators the visibility they need.</p></div>
        <div class="landing-feature-grid">
            <article class="landing-feature"><span class="landing-feature-icon"><Icon Name="shield" /></span><h3>Permission-gated SQL</h3><p>Statements are analysed and checked against effective permissions before they reach a database.</p></article>
            <article class="landing-feature"><span class="landing-feature-icon"><Icon Name="clock" /></span><h3>Access on your terms</h3><p>Manage role and user grants, approve requests and set time windows for temporary access.</p></article>
            <article class="landing-feature"><span class="landing-feature-icon"><Icon Name="list" /></span><h3>Accountability built in</h3><p>Queries require an audit record before execution, giving your team a trail of activity.</p></article>
            <article class="landing-feature"><span class="landing-feature-icon"><Icon Name="terminal" /></span><h3>A workspace for SQL</h3><p>Explore database objects, write and save queries, and review results in one place.</p></article>
            <article class="landing-feature"><span class="landing-feature-icon"><Icon Name="check" /></span><h3>Requests and approvals</h3><p>Request database access or submit scripts for administrators to review.</p></article>
            <article class="landing-feature"><span class="landing-feature-icon"><Icon Name="table" /></span><h3>Results you can use</h3><p>Review results in a grid and export CSV when you have export permission.</p></article>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="landing-section" aria-labelledby="workspace-title">
        <div class="landing-section-head"><span class="landing-kicker">THE WORKSPACE</span><h2 id="workspace-title">From SQL to results in one place.</h2><p>Browse objects, run permitted queries and inspect results without sharing database credentials with every user.</p></div>
        <figure class="landing-screenshot">
            <img src="/images/query-workspace.jpeg" alt="Query Gate workspace showing a SQL query and two sample order results" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Query workspace shown with fictional sample data.</figcaption>
        </figure>
    </section>
    <section class="landing-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
        <div class="landing-section-head"><span class="landing-kicker">HOW IT WORKS</span><h2 id="workflow-title">Four steps to governed access.</h2></div>
        <ol class="landing-steps">
            <li><span>01</span><h3>Register a database</h3><p>An administrator connects a SQL Server database using a dedicated account.</p></li>
            <li><span>02</span><h3>Grant access</h3><p>Configure role or user permissions, including optional time windows, or review access requests.</p></li>
            <li><span>03</span><h3>Run checked SQL</h3><p>Users work in the query workspace. The SQL gate checks statements and permissions before execution.</p></li>
            <li><span>04</span><h3>Review activity</h3><p>Queries require an audit record before execution. Review activity in the audit log.</p></li>
        </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="landing-section" aria-labelledby="audiences-title">
        <div class="landing-section-head"><span class="landing-kicker">BUILT FOR TEAMS</span><h2 id="audiences-title">A shared workflow, different responsibilities.</h2></div>
        <div class="landing-audience-grid">
            <article><h3>Developers</h3><p>Explore and query databases with the access needed for the task.</p></article>
            <article><h3>QA and testers</h3><p>Inspect test data and request the permissions needed for verification.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Administrators</h3><p>Register databases, manage access and review requests.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Auditors</h3><p>Review audit logs and the access matrix for visibility into activity and permissions.</p></article>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="landing-section landing-start" aria-labelledby="start-title">
        <div class="landing-section-head"><span class="landing-kicker">GET STARTED</span><h2 id="start-title">Choose where to run Query Gate.</h2><p>Start with a reachable SQL Server application database, initial administrator credentials and production secrets. Hosting requires HTTPS and persistent data protection keys.</p></div>
        <p>Use Docker with Compose, or publish with the .NET 10 SDK for your chosen host. Follow the deployment guide for migrations, certificates and secure configuration.</p>
        <div class="landing-link-list" aria-label="Deployment guides">
            <a href="/documentation#docker">Docker</a><a href="/documentation#iis">IIS</a><a href="/documentation#azure">Azure App Service</a><a href="/documentation#linux">Linux server</a>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="landing-section landing-info-grid" aria-label="Project information">
        <article class="landing-info-card">
            <span class="landing-kicker">OPEN SOURCE</span><h2>Build with the community.</h2>
            <p>Explore the code, report an issue or contribute an improvement. Start with the contribution guide for local setup and tests.</p>
            <div class="landing-link-list"><a href="https://github.com/arjunreddy-001/query-gate">GitHub repository</a><a href="https://github.com/arjunreddy-001/query-gate/issues">Issues</a><a href="https://github.com/arjunreddy-001/query-gate/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Contributing</a><a href="https://github.com/arjunreddy-001/query-gate/blob/main/LICENSE">License</a></div>
        </article>
        <article class="landing-info-card">
            <span class="landing-kicker">SECURITY AND SCOPE</span><h2>Use guardrails with least privilege.</h2>
            <p>Application permissions complement SQL Server permissions. Use dedicated least-privilege database accounts, HTTPS, protected secrets and secure backups.</p>
            <p>Query Gate targets SQL Server. CSV is the only export format, object-level permission scope is not supported, and LocalDB is untested.</p>
            <a href="/documentation#configuration">Read deployment and security guidance</a>
        </article>
    </section>
</div>
